..h1 S’mores Tart

Based on a recipe by Claire Saffitz from her book |What’s for Dessert|, but using the crust from |Brian Lagerstrom’s Key Lime Pie|, with small modifications to both.

**NOTE: This is a draft.**

..author Colin Chan
..time ?? hours
..yield 1 tart

::recipe

    ..recipe-part Crust

    ..* `230 g` graham crackers
    ..* `25 g` milk powder
    ..* `30 g` sugar
    ..* `4 g` salt
    ..* `? g` cardamom powder
    ..* `65 g` unsalted butter, melted but not hot
    ..* `65 g` heavy cream

    ..# Pulse the graham crackers, milk powder, sugar, and salt in a food processor until they have a sandy texture.

    ..# Pour in the butter and cream while spinning until the texture is like damp sand (holds together when you squeeze).

    ..# Press into a greased pie pan and bake at 375°F for 12(?) minutes (light golden brown color).

    ..# Cool completely.


    ..recipe-part Ganache

    ..* `170 g` chocolate (64–70% cacao)
    ..* `? g (generous pinch)` salt
    ..* `2 Tbsp` unsalted butter
    ..* `3/4 c` heavy cream

    ..#(start=5) Heat the cream to ?? temp (too hot, chocolate breaks).

    ..# Pour the cream over the chocolate, salt, and butter, and let sit for 5 minutes to melt the chocolate.

    ..# Whisk gently, starting in the center and working outward, until the mixture is completely smooth.

    ..* `1/2 c` heavy cream
    
    ..#(start=8) Whip to medium peaks.

    ..# Beat the ganache until it thickens (4 minutes).

    ..# Fold in the whipped cream.

    ..# Spread into the crust and set aside uncovered to set (>15 minutes).


    ..recipe-part Marshmallow

    ..* `1/4 c` cold water
    ..* `2.5 tsp (1 packet)` gelatin

    ..#(start=11) Hydrate the gelatin for 10 minutes.

    ..# Melt the gelatin in a double-boiler.

    ..# Remove from the heat and let cool for 1 minute.

    ..* `133 g` sugar
    ..* `2 Tbsp` light corn syrup
    ..* `105 g (3)` egg whites
    ..* `1/8 tsp` cream of tartar
    ..* `? g (generous pinch)` salt

    ..#(start=14) Add the sugar, corn syrup, egg whites, cream of tartar, and salt, and whisk continuously until the sugar fully dissolves.

    ..# Whisk to 160°F over the double-boiler to pasteurize.

    ..# Beat to stiff peaks (7–9 minutes).

    ..* `1 Tbsp` vanilla

    ..#(start=17) Beat in vanilla.

    ..# Scrape onto the tart and swirl.

    ..# Let sit uncovered until the marshmallow is firm (>2 hours).
